  "job_B1.3.24_20251001_193208": {
    "text": "III KAL AUGUSTI, NATALIS SANCTORUM ABDON ET SENNES.\nON DECIES DAGVM \u00f0\u00e6S DEOFLICAN CASERES w\u00e6ron twegen kyningas on Crist gelyfde, Abdon\n\u00d0a asprang heora word to \u00f0am w\u00e6lhreowan casere \u00fee \u00f0a ana geweold ealles middaneardes, and ealle\n\u00dea asende Decius to \u00feam fores\u00e6dum cyningum, and het hi gebringan on bendum to him, wolde hi\nHw\u00e6t \u00fea cwelleras \u00fea \u00fea cynincgas gebundon, and on isenum racenteagum to \u00f0am arleasan gebrohton\nDecius \u00fea het \u00fea halgan cyningas his godum geoffrian, ac hi andwyrdon \u00feus, We offria\u00f0 ure lac \u00feam\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Decius, se deofles biggenga, \u00feysum is to gearcigenne \u00fea re\u00feestan wita.\nAbdon and Sennes him andwyrdon \u00f0us, Hw\u00e6s abitst \u00feu casere?\nCy\u00f0 hw\u00e6t \u00feu wylle, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu wite so\u00f0lice \u00fe\u00e6t we orsorge syndon on urum H\u00e6lende Criste, \u00fee h\u00e6f\u00f0 \u00fea\n\u00dea on \u00feam o\u00f0rum d\u00e6ge het Decius se casere l\u00e6tan leon and beran to \u00feam geleaffullum cynegum, \u00fe\u00e6t hi\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Ualerianus to \u00feam cynegum \u00feus, Beorga\u00f0 eowrum gebyrdum, and buga\u00f0 to urum godum, and\nAbdon and Sennes s\u00e6don \u00feam arleasan, We gebidda\u00f0 us to Drihtne gebigdum limum, and we n\u00e6fre ne\n\u00dea het Ualerianus \u00f0a halgan unscrydan, and l\u00e6dan swa nocode to \u00f0\u00e6re sunnan anlicnysse, for\u00f0an \u00f0e hi\n\u00dea cw\u00e6don \u00f0a cynegas to \u00feam cwellere \u00f0us, Do \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu don wylt.\nAnd se dema het beswingan \u00fea halgan hetelice swy\u00f0e mi\u00f0 leadenum swipum, and l\u00e6dde hi sy\u00f0\u00f0an to\n\u00dea urnon \u00fea deor egeslice grymetende to \u00fe\u00e6re halgena fotum, swylce hi fry\u00f0es b\u00e6don, and noldon\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Ualerianus to \u00f0am cempum \u00feus, Heora drycr\u00e6ft is gesyne swutollice on \u00f0ysum.\nAnd he wear\u00f0 swy\u00f0e gram for \u00fe\u00e6re deora ware, and het \u00f0a \u00e6t nextan \u00fea h\u00e6\u00f0enan cwelleras ingan mid\n\u00dea \u00f0e \u00feis gedon w\u00e6s, \u00fea het se dema teon \u00fe\u00e6ra halgena lic to \u00f0am h\u00e6\u00feengilde, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0a Cristenan\n\u00d0a \u00e6fter \u00ferym dagum, com sum diacon \u00fe\u00e6r to, Quirinus gehaten, and he \u00f0a halgan lic nihtes gel\u00e6hte,\nAnd hi mannum \u00fe\u00e6r bediglode lagon to langum fyrste, o\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t Constantinus, se Cristene casere, eft to\nGe habba\u00f0 nu gehyrod hu \u00f0a halgan cyningas heora cynedom forsawon for Cristes geleafan and heora\nNima\u00f0 eow bysne be \u00f0am, \u00fe\u00e6t ge ne bugon fram Criste for \u00e6nigre earfo\u00f0nysse, \u00fe\u00e6t ge \u00fe\u00e6t ece lif\nITEM ALIA.\nNu we spr\u00e6con be cynegum we willa\u00f0 \u00feysne cwyde gelencgan, and be sumum cynincge eow cy\u00f0an git,\nAnd se l\u00e6g beddryda on \u00f0am timan \u00fee se h\u00e6lend on \u00feysum life w\u00e6s.\nHe h\u00e6fde geaxod be \u00f0\u00e6s h\u00e6lendes wundrum, and sende \u00f0a ardlice \u00feis \u00e6rendgewrit him to, Abgarus\nIc h\u00e6bbe gehyred be \u00f0e, hu \u00f0u geh\u00e6lst \u00f0a untruman, blinde and healte, and bedrydan ar\u00e6st; hreoflige\nNu cw\u00e6\u00f0 ic on minum mode, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0u eart \u00e6lmihtig God, o\u00f0\u00f0e Godes sunu, \u00f0e sylf come to mannum,\nMe is eac ges\u00e6d \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0a iudeiscan syrwia\u00f0, and runia\u00f0 him betwynan hu hi \u00fee ber\u00e6dan magon, and ic\n\u00dea awrat se h\u00e6lend him sylf \u00feis gewrit, and asende \u00f0am cynincge \u00f0us cw\u00e6\u00f0ende him to, Beatus es qui\nHit is awriten be me on witegungbocum, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0a \u00fee me geseo\u00f0 hi ne gelyfa\u00f0 on me, and \u00fea \u00fee me ne\nBe \u00feam \u00fee \u00f0u awrite to me \u00fe\u00e6t ic come to \u00fee, ic sceal \u00e6rest afyllan \u00fea \u00feincg \u00fee ic fore asend eom and\nAnd ic asende to \u00f0e, sy\u00f0\u00f0an ic genumen beo, \u00e6nne minra leorningcnihta, \u00fee gelacnia\u00f0 \u00feine\n\u00deis gewrit com \u00fea to \u00feam cyninge sona, and se H\u00e6lend foresceawode sy\u00f0\u00f0an he to heofonum astah,\nHe com \u00f0a \u00feurh Godes sande to \u00fe\u00e6re fores\u00e6dan byrig, and geh\u00e6lde \u00feone untrumne on \u00fe\u00e6s H\u00e6lendes\n\u00dea gemunde se cyning hw\u00e6t Crist him \u00e6r behet, and het him to gefeccan \u00feone fores\u00e6dan Tatheum, se\nAnd mid \u00f0am he ineode, \u00fea aras se cyning and feoll to his fotum \u00e6tforan his \u00f0egnum, for\u00f0an \u00fee he\n\u00dea andwyrde se Tatheus \u00f0am arwur\u00f0an cyninge \u00feus, For\u00f0an \u00f0e \u00feu rihtlice gelyfdest on \u00feone \u00f0e me\nAbgarus him andwyrde anr\u00e6dlice and cw\u00e6\u00f0, To \u00feam swy\u00f0e ic gelyfe on \u00feone lyfigendan H\u00e6lend,\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Tatheus him to, Crist ure h\u00e6lend wolde his f\u00e6der willan gefyllan, and eft faran to him.\nAbgarus cw\u00e6\u00f0 him eft to, Ic wat eall be \u00feam, and ic on hine gelyfe, and on his halgan f\u00e6der.\nTatheus cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fea gyt to \u00f0am wanhalan cyninge, for\u00fei ic sette mine hand on \u00f0\u00e6s h\u00e6lendes naman ofer\nAbgarus \u00fea wundrode \u00fe\u00e6t he wear\u00f0 geh\u00e6led butan l\u00e6cewyrtum, \u00feurh \u00f0\u00e6s h\u00e6lendes word, swa swa he\nTatheus eac si\u00f0\u00f0an sumne mann geh\u00e6lde fram \u00feam micclan fotadle, and fela o\u00f0re menn on \u00fe\u00e6re byrig\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 Abgarus him to, On Cristes mihte \u00feu wyrcst \u00feas micclan wundra, and we ealle \u00f0\u00e6s\nSege me, ic \u00fee bidde, so\u00f0 be \u00f0am H\u00e6lende, hu he to mannum come, and of middanearde ferde.\nTatheus andwyrde Abgare and cw\u00e6\u00f0, Ic eom asend to bodigenne hat \u00feine burhware cuman ealle\n\u00dea het se cynincg cuman his ceastergewaran, and Tatheus him bodade bealdlice be Criste, and him\n\u00c6fter \u00f0yssere bodunge bead se cyning \u00feam bydele goldes and seolfres godne d\u00e6l to lace, ac he nolde\n\u00deis w\u00e6s \u00feus geworden, and \u00fe\u00e6r wunode a sy\u00f0\u00f0an se so\u00f0a geleafa on \u00fe\u00e6re landleode, \u00feam H\u00e6lende to",
